{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB01177 - MONDO_20320",
  "verbalization": "Idarubicin is associated with Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation through a shared pathway involving Mitoxantrone, which is indicated for a variety of leukemias, including those with Npm1, Cebpa, or Inv3(p21;q26.2) mutations. The evidence suggests that Idarubicin may exert its therapeutic effect through a mechanism that leads to the activation of Mitoxantrone, which in turn is effective against Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation. This relationship is supported by the high scores in the visible paths, indicating a strong and consistent association across different genetic subtypes of the disease. The presence of Mitoxantrone as a common target in these pathways implies a potential mechanism of action that involves the induction of apoptosis or other cellular processes in leukemic cells. The integration of these paths highlights the role of Mitoxantrone as a bridge between Idarubicin and the disease, suggesting a possible synergistic or additive effect in treating this form of leukemia.",
